# GIT1 (2026-07-19) — machine and tooling artefacts.
#
# These were previously excluded ONLY by a machine-level /etc/.gitignore on the
# Replit host, not by the repository. That is not portable: on any other machine
# — a laptop, a CI runner, a fresh clone — `.cache/` and friends are committable,
# and a cache directory is exactly the kind of thing that gets swept up by a
# broad `git add` at the end of a long session. Declaring them here makes the
# exclusion a property of the repository rather than of one host.
.env.*
!.env.example
.cache/
.tmp/
*.local
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.playwright/
ms-playwright/
*.log
